## 13. Menus, dialogs, panels and feedback

### Dropdown

Minimum width 160px, 14px font, 4px vertical padding, 8px radius, theme surface, 1px theme border and subtle shadow. Item hover uses the tertiary surface. Disabled items are noninteractive. Support group dividers, aligned placement, keyboard controls and viewport collision handling. At ≤600px topbar menus become full-width.

### Modal

Normal width 500px, small 300px, large 800px, XL 1140px from Bootstrap source sizing. Surface follows the theme, radius 16px. Header/body padding 24px; footer padding 20px with child margins accounting for an 8px gap. Variants include centered, scrollable, top/bottom, static backdrop, toggling between modals, fullscreen and breakpoint fullscreen.

Dialog fade/translation is 300ms ease-out, backdrop fade 150ms. Backdrop uses the theme emphasis color at 50% layer opacity. Do not treat a mid-animation computed opacity of zero as final design. Modal opening was directly tested. Required target behavior: focus trap, Escape/backdrop policy, focus restoration, body scroll lock, accessible label and scrollable body. Static backdrop must not close on outside click. Destructive confirmation waits for the real backend result. Never show success after a failed request.

### Offcanvas

Settings panel opens from the right, measured width 280px, theme surface, no border in its markup, 300ms ease-in-out translation. Header contains title/Close; body scrolls; footer contains Reset. Activity panel uses a timeline with avatars, attachments, status and timestamps; populate it from the target audit feed. Generic start/end/top/bottom/responsive variants are in the component catalog; not every drawer has the settings panel's 280px width.

### Settings state

Root attributes: `data-bs-theme`, `data-topbar-color`, `data-menu-color`, `data-menu-size`. Defaults: light/light/dark/sm-hover-active. Controls cover global Light/Dark, topbar Light/Dark, menu Light/Dark, and Default/Condensed/Hidden/Small Hover Active/Small Hover. Reset restores defaults.

Reference persists JSON in **sessionStorage `__LARKON_CONFIG__`**. The target may namespace the key or use its own preference API; document any change in persistence duration. Initialize before paint or through an SSR-compatible bootstrap to avoid a flash. Guard invalid saved JSON. A viewport change must not erase the preferred desktop menu mode.

### Feedback components

- Alerts: semantic filled/subtle/outline/dismissible variants. Show real messages, not the demo's server warning.
- Badges: rounded/pill, status/dot/count; standard padding `.3em .6em`, weight 600, line-height 1.
- Progress: semantic track/bar, stacked/striped/animated variants and accessible numeric value.
- Spinners: border/grow, size/color variants and screen-reader label; no permanent loading.
- Placeholders: reserve content bounds while fetching.
- Toasts: Bootstrap/Toastify variants, position/duration/Close and stop-on-focus behavior. Use target notifications.
- Tooltips/popovers: hover/focus/click as appropriate; essential information cannot depend on hover alone.
